<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IV </span><span id="S4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Experiments</span></h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span> </span><span id="S4.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Experimental Setup</span></h3>

<section id="S4.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S4.SS1.SSS1.4" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span>1 </span>Datasets</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In our experiments, we train all models on the Adobe240 dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib101" title="" class="ltx_ref">101</a>]</cite> which contains 133 video sequences, where 100 for training, 16 for validation, and 17 for testing <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite>. We evaluate the performance of our models on both synthetic Adobe240 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib101" title="" class="ltx_ref">101</a>]</cite> and GoPro <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite> datasets and real-world datasets including BS-ERGB <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib82" title="" class="ltx_ref">82</a>]</cite> and ALPIX-VSR <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>. For synthetic events, we use the event simulation method Vid2E <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib102" title="" class="ltx_ref">102</a>]</cite> to generate the event data. Given a spatial scale <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> and a temporal scale <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, we select consecutive <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t+1)</annotation></semantics></math> frames as a clip. The first and last frames for <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s:1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s:1</annotation></semantics></math> bicubic downsampling are used as the LR and LFR inputs fed into the network to generate the HR and HFR frame sequences, respectively, and the original <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t+1)</annotation></semantics></math> frames serve as the ground truth (GT). Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">67</a>]</cite>, the event voxels are bicubic-downsampled as the LR event inputs, thus ensuring the spatial size is aligned with the LR frames.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE I: </span>The detailed implementation settings of the cross-derivative training strategy (Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ III-E2 Cross-Derivative Training Strategy ‣ III-E EvEnhancerPlus ‣ III Proposed Method ‣ Towards Robust and Generalizable Continuous Space-Time Video Super-Resolution with Events" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) in our <span id="S4.T1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">EvEnhancerPlus</span>.</figcaption>
